event: search
data: {"query":"iPad Air vs iPad Pro for drawing, which one and how much?","freshness":"any","results":[{"title":"2024 iPad Air vs. iPad Pro: Which Tablet Should You Buy? | PCMag","url":"https://www.pcmag.com/comparisons/2024-ipad-air-vs-ipad-pro-which-tablet-should-you-buy","snippet":"Apple's latest versions of the iPad Air ($599) and iPad Pro ($999) make them more powerful and versatile than ever. Both tablets are available with an 11-inch or 13-inch screen, have cutting-edge processors, and support all the creative accessories you could want. But before you rush to order either, you need to know…","date":"2024-12-10T15:33:57.000Z","content":"Apple's latest versions of the iPad Air ($599) and iPad Pro ($999) make them more powerful and versatile than ever. Both tablets are available with an 11-inch or 13-inch screen, have cutting-edge processors, and support all the creative accessories you could want. But before you rush to order either, you need to know how they stack up against one another. We're here to help.\nIn this comparison, we explain all the important differences below. If you already know which model best fits your needs, the iPad Air and iPad Pro are widely available for delivery or in-store pickup.\nThe 11-inch iPad Air costs $599 for 128GB of storage, $699 for 256GB, $899 for 512GB, or $1,099 for 1TB. The starting price is the same as for the previous iteration, though with a nice bump up from 64GB. The 13-inch version costs $200 more across the board. If you want cellular connectivity, prepare to shell out another $150.\nMeanwhile, the 11-inch iPad Pro comes in at $999 for 256GB of storage, $1,199 for 512GB, $1,599 for 1TB, and $1,999 for 2TB. The base model costs $200 more than the prior model. If you want a larger 13-inch screen or 5G support, those upgrades respectively cost $300 and $200. Opting for the Nano-texture Glass on the 1TB and 2TB models adds another $100. Like with the Air, Apple doubled the base storage here, but in the case of the Pro, it also raised the price.\nBoth are pricey (especially since accessories can add a few extra hundred dollars), though the iPad Air remains the more reasonably priced choice of the two.\nThe 11-inch iPad Air measures 9.74 by 7.02 by 0.24 inches (HWD) and weighs 1.02 pounds. It's a bit thicker and heavier than the 11-inch iPad Pro (9.83 by 6.99 by 0.21 inches, 0.98 pounds). It's a similar story with the 13-inch iPad Air (11.04 by 8.46 by 0.24 inches, 1.36 pounds) and iPad Pro (11.09 by 8.48 by 0.20 inches, 1.28 pounds). The design of the tablets is more or less identical, with only small things setting them apart visually. The most obvious difference is the camera module, which is narrower on the Air and more square on the Pro.","domain":"pcmag.com","engines":["web"]},{"title":"iPad Air (1st generation)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IPad_Air_(1st_generation)","snippet":"iPad Air (1st generation)\nDiscontinued 64 GB & 128 GB: October 16, 2014 16 GB & 32 GB: March 21, 2016\nSystem on a chip Apple A7 with 64-bit architecture and Apple M7 motion co-processor\nMemory 1 GB LPDDR3 RAM [ 2 ]\nStorage 16, 32, 64, 128 GB [ a ] flash memory\nDisplay 9.7 inches (250 mm) 2,048 × 1,536 px color IPS dis…","date":"2026-08-09T00:30:12.000Z","content":"iPad Air (1st generation)\nDiscontinued 64 GB & 128 GB: October 16, 2014 16 GB & 32 GB: March 21, 2016\nSystem on a chip Apple A7 with 64-bit architecture and Apple M7 motion co-processor\nMemory 1 GB LPDDR3 RAM [ 2 ]\nStorage 16, 32, 64, 128 GB [ a ] flash memory\nDisplay 9.7 inches (250 mm) 2,048 × 1,536 px color IPS display , [ 3 ] (264 ppi ) with a 4:3 aspect ratio, oleophobic coating\nInput Multi-touch screen , headset controls , M7 motion co-processor, proximity and ambient light sensors, 3-axis accelerometer , 3-axis gyroscope , digital compass , dual microphone\nCamera Front : 1.2 MP, 720p HD Rear : OmniVision Technologies OV5650 5.0 MP AF, iSight with Five Element Lens, Hybrid IR filter , video stabilisation, face detection, HDR, ƒ/2.4 aperture\nConnectivity Wi-Fi and Wi-Fi + Cellular: Wi-Fi 802.11 a / b / g / n at 2.4 GHz and 5 GHz and MIMO Bluetooth 4.0 Wi-Fi + Cellular: GPS & GLONASS GSM UMTS / HSDPA 850, 1700, 1900, 2100 MHz GSM / EDGE 850, 900, 1800, 1900 MHz CDMA CDMA / EV-DO Rev. A and B. 800, 1900 MHz LTE Multiple bands A1475 : 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 7, 8, 13, 17, 18, 19, 20, 25, 26; A1476 : 1, 2, 3, 5, 7, 8, 18, 19, 20 and TD-LTE 38, 39, 40\nPower Built-in rechargeable Li-Po battery 8,827 mAh 3.73 V 32.9 W⋅h (118 kJ) [ 4 ]\nOnline services App Store , iTunes Store , iBookstore , iCloud , Game Center\nDimensions 240 mm (9.4 in) (h) 169.5 mm (6.67 in) (w) 7.5 mm (0.30 in) (d)\nWeight Wi-Fi: 469 g (1.034 lb) Wi-Fi + Cellular: 478 g (1.054 lb)\nPredecessor iPad (4th generation)\nWebsite Apple - iPad Air at the Wayback Machine (archived December 14, 2013)","domain":"en.wikipedia.org","engines":["web"]},{"title":"iPad Air — official store","url":"https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-ipad/ipad-air","snippet":"iPad Air 11-inch (M4): From $749 on apple.com (official store price)","domain":"apple.com","engines":["web"],"content":"iPad Air 11-inch (M4): From $749 on apple.com (official store price)\n\nShop iPad Air - Apple {\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"Product\",\"name\":\"iPad Air 13-inch (M4)\",\"url\":\"https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-ipad/ipad-air\",\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://www.apple.com/shop/buy-ipad/ipad-air\",\"offers\":[{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\"priceCurrency\":\"USD\",\"price\":1199.00,\"sku\":\"MH9J4LL/A\",\"shippingDetails\":{\"@type\":\"OfferShippingDetails\",\"shippingRate\":{\"@type\":\"MonetaryAmount\",\"value\":0,\"currency\":\"USD\"}},\"hasMerchantReturnPolicy\":{\"@type\":\"MerchantReturnPolicy\",\"applicableCountry\":\"US\",\"returnPolicyCategory\":\"https://schema.org/MerchantReturnFiniteReturnWindow\",\"merchantReturnDays\":14,\"returnMethod\":\"https://schema.org/ReturnByMail\",\"returnFees\":\"https://schema.org/FreeReturn\"}},{\"@type\":\"Offer\",\